<%# #936 — the browser-tab and bookmark icons.

    A partial rather than duplicated markup: the application and login layouts
    both need these, and an icon set that is right on one screen and stale on
    the other is the kind of drift nobody notices until a bookmark looks wrong.

    Order matters. A browser takes the LAST icon link it understands, so the
    .ico is declared first as the universal fallback and the SVG after it, which
    lets a modern browser scale the mark on a high-DPI tab while an older one
    still finds something it can render.

    Paths are literal rather than `asset_path`: these live in `public/`, not the
    asset pipeline, because /favicon.ico is a fixed location browsers request
    with no link element at all — a digested filename could never satisfy that.
%>
<link rel="icon" href="/favicon.ico" sizes="32x32">
<link rel="icon" href="/icon.svg" type="image/svg+xml">
<link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="/apple-touch-icon.png">
